<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK steps in to support won vs dollar - dealers.</title>
<headline>BOK steps in to support won vs dollar - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea (BOK) intervened in early trading on Thursday to support the falling won at the 829.90 level against the dollar, dealers said.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the won bounced back to 828.30 after the bank's dollar selling.</p>
<p>&quot;The bullish sentiment towards the dollar and import deals were boosting the dollar before the intervention,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Traders said the central bank is expected to intervene again if the won retreats back to around the 830 level.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
